# Plasma Disc

A self-contained plasma-globe page. No build step, no dependencies. GitHub Pages serves `index.html` at https://michael714.github.io/plasma-disc/.

## Source of truth

- Edit `index.html` in place. It is the live app.
- Do not rewrite, "clean up," or replace it with a new HTML file. A previous rewrite dropped the generated Plasma Buzz audio.
- Do not add a bundler, framework, or extra JS/CSS files unless explicitly asked.

## Audio (do not collapse these)

- **Plasma Buzz** is synthesized Web Audio (detuned oscillators + filtered noise). It is on by default and unlocks on first pointer/key gesture (autoplay policy).
- Route buzz through `sfxMasterGain` → destination. **Never** connect it to `analyser`.
- `analyser` is only for external music (microphone or a local file) so the visuals can pulse without the buzz feeding back into itself.
- Keep `updateBuzz()` using `setTargetAtTime` glides, not stepped gain. Discrete clicks sound mechanical.

```javascript
// ❌ BAD — buzz drives the visual analyser
sfxMasterGain.connect(analyser);

// ✅ GOOD — music/mic only into analyser; buzz is a separate bus
audioSource.connect(analyser);
sfxMasterGain.connect(audioCtx.destination);
```

## Visuals

Keep fingertip attraction (bolts bend toward pointer/touch), concentric color bands, and fullscreen/TV-cast friendly UI (controls auto-hide).

## Quality tiers (keep all three)

Bolts use additive glow strokes, never canvas `shadowBlur` (CPU-heavy; it made a Pi 400 unusable). Do not CSS-blur the whole `<canvas>` — that softens the rim and color bands.

| Tier | When | Look |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **high** | Default on capable machines | Full DPR (capped at 2), 13 bolts, branches, texture |
| **lite** | ARM Linux / Raspberry / ≤2 cores, or frames stay slow | Same on-screen size as high; cap **backing-store** pixels (`maxBackingPx`), not CSS size. Keep branches, glow halo, and similar bolt count |
| **ultra** | Only if lite still misses frame time | Smaller backing store, fewer bolts, no branches, ~30fps |

URL overrides (keep these — they are how we compare without a Pi):

- `https://michael714.github.io/plasma-disc/` — high
- `…/plasma-disc/?lite` — lite
- `…/plasma-disc/?ultra` — ultra

Do not regress lite to a small, unbranched 7-bolt disc. That was tried and looked too plain next to high. Ultra is the sparse emergency tier.

`canvas.dataset.quality` is `"high"` / `"lite"` / `"ultra"`. Auto-detect may drop high → lite → ultra; it must not bounce back up.

## Deploy

Push to `main`. `.github/workflows/deploy.yml` republishes Pages automatically. Do not switch Pages to "Deploy from a branch" unless asked.
